# Two samplers record their own sample numbers, so every line halsampler prints
# says which sample it is.  "lossy" has a ring of two on a 100 us thread: the
# stream bridge polls about once a millisecond, so it loses samples all the
# time.  "roomy" holds ten seconds and must lose none.
load sampler <lossy> depth=2 cfg=s
load sampler <roomy> depth=100000 cfg=s
newthread fast 100000
addf lossy fast
addf roomy fast
net lossy-num lossy.sample-num => lossy.pin.0
net roomy-num roomy.sample-num => roomy.pin.0
